## Wave 2: Config (estimated ~210 failures, moderate effort)

t1300-config is the single biggest failure source in the entire t1 family: 206 of 497 tests fail.

Config is foundational — other tests depend on correct config parsing. Fixing this likely has cascading benefits across the whole test suite.

**Likely failure areas** (based on typical git config complexity):
- Multivar handling (get-all, unset-all, replace-all)
- Section/subsection edge cases
- Global/system config file resolution
- Config types (bool, int, expiry-date, color)
- Conditional includes (gitdir, onbranch)
- NUL-terminated output (--null flag)
- Config editing (--add, --unset, --rename-section, --remove-section)

**Approach**: Run t1300 in isolation, categorize failures by feature, fix in batches.

